Expanded story:
Amy flips a skillet over the stove as the scent of sizzling bacon fills the kitchen. She ladles eggs into bowls for Will and Amber, humming softly while the children giggle at their tiny cereal boats.

A sudden thump on the front door shatters her rhythm. A zombie—its tattered shirt hanging off one shoulder—steps inside, its eyes fixed on the family. Amy grabs a toddler’s hand, pulls Will toward the back bedroom closet and pushes Amber into the hallway. She slams the closet door behind them and runs back to the kitchen.

She darts through the pantry, fingers brushing against a hidden panel in the wall. The panel slides open with a click, revealing an arsenal: a gleaming pistol on a hook and a katana tucked beneath it. Amy pulls out both weapons, her breath steadying as she hears another groan from the hallway.

The first zombie lunges at her from behind the fridge; Amy swings the katana in one swift arc, severing its head. A second zombie shuffles into view by the stove, and with a quick pull of the trigger, its skull cracks against the countertop. The third creeps out from the back door—its limbs clattering on the tiles—and she shoots it before it can reach her.

More zombies burst in: one slams through the kitchen window, another rolls across the floorboards. Amy ducks behind the stove, firing shots and slicing with the katana between each staggered attack. The rhythm of crunching flesh and gunfire fills the house as she dispatches them all—one after another—until only a single zombie remains in the doorway.

She raises her pistol, takes aim, and pulls the trigger; the last zombie collapses into a splattered heap. Amy exhales sharply, then turns toward the back bedroom closet where Will’s small voice calls for her. She steps out of the kitchen, grabs Will’s hand, and pulls Amber from the hallway. Together they step back into the safety of their hidden room, breathing in relief as the house falls silent once more.
